1
00:00:02,420 --> 00:00:03,960
Hey, Ben, you seen Grandma yet?

2
00:00:04,520 --> 00:00:05,540
I'm not sure.

3
00:00:05,740 --> 00:00:09,580
Usually it's easy to spot her, but everybody on this boat has gray hair.

4
00:00:11,380 --> 00:00:12,200
Relax, honey.

5
00:00:12,240 --> 00:00:14,640
I'm sure your mother had a great time.

6
00:00:15,480 --> 00:00:15,800
Whoa!

7
00:00:16,540 --> 00:00:17,580
Well, you see her, Ben?

8
00:00:17,960 --> 00:00:21,220
No, but I do see a blonde fox in a really tight red dress.

9
00:00:22,340 --> 00:00:24,160
She's kissing an old bald guy.

10
00:00:26,120 --> 00:00:29,320
Hey, almost all the guys are bald.

11
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:32,220
Half the boat's unloaded.

12
00:00:32,240 --> 00:00:33,300
Maggie, where is she?

13
00:00:34,560 --> 00:00:36,100
You know, she's never traveled alone.

14
00:00:36,120 --> 00:00:38,300
I think maybe this is just too close to Dad's funeral.

15
00:00:38,600 --> 00:00:40,660
Honey, a year of mourning is enough.

16
00:00:42,040 --> 00:00:43,880
Well, maybe it's just too much for her.

17
00:00:43,880 --> 00:00:45,440
Maybe I shouldn't have sent her on this cruise.

18
00:00:45,660 --> 00:00:47,260
Oh, give her some credit, Jason.

19
00:00:47,260 --> 00:00:48,760
She could take care of herself.

20
00:00:49,340 --> 00:00:51,480
I should have listened when she said she'd rather just be

21
00:00:51,480 --> 00:00:53,780
at home staring at the walls and remembering Dad.

22
00:00:54,180 --> 00:00:56,220
Oh, honey, she didn't know what she was saying,

23
00:00:56,240 --> 00:00:58,320
and she needed you to step in and take care of her.

24
00:00:58,420 --> 00:01:00,360
Oh, first you say she's a good girl, she can take care of herself,

25
00:01:00,440 --> 00:01:02,440
then you say, it's a good thing I stepped in.

26
00:01:02,600 --> 00:01:04,480
Let's have some consistency, Maggie.

27
00:01:06,980 --> 00:01:09,720
I'm just saying to not get carried away.

28
00:01:10,700 --> 00:01:14,320
You know, Ethel Merman went through the exactly the same thing as your mom

29
00:01:14,320 --> 00:01:17,560
when she set sail on the love boat and she ended her cruise with Gene Rayburn.

30
00:01:20,540 --> 00:01:22,660
And to think they canceled that show.

31
00:01:25,160 --> 00:01:27,120
Hey, there's the guy with hair.

32
00:01:28,300 --> 00:01:28,820
Okay.

33
00:01:29,320 --> 00:01:30,380
Nice wig.

34
00:01:30,580 --> 00:01:32,600
If you're not gonna look for Grandma, give me the binoculars.

35
00:01:32,700 --> 00:01:33,900
Oh Jason, there she is.

36
00:01:34,240 --> 00:01:34,380
Irma!

37
00:01:34,780 --> 00:01:35,140
Where?

38
00:01:35,580 --> 00:01:36,240
Where is she?

39
00:01:36,260 --> 00:01:37,140
On the gateway.

40
00:01:37,360 --> 00:01:37,800
Irma!

41
00:01:38,380 --> 00:01:41,340
The only woman on the gangway is that blonde who's...

42
00:01:41,340 --> 00:01:42,020
Oh my God!

43
00:01:49,180 --> 00:01:50,120
How is that?

44
00:01:50,840 --> 00:01:51,320
I didn't even...

45
00:01:51,320 --> 00:01:53,660
Stop stammering and kiss your mother.

46
00:01:55,140 --> 00:01:57,100
Oh Irma, you look great.

47
00:01:57,100 --> 00:01:59,800
Well, I should for what I paid for it.

48
00:01:59,960 --> 00:02:00,620
Yeah, I was like...

49
00:02:00,620 --> 00:02:02,860
Okay, okay, for what you paid for it.

50
00:02:02,880 --> 00:02:03,720
Well, that doesn't end...

51
00:02:03,720 --> 00:02:05,620
Benjamin! Benjamin!

52
00:02:06,380 --> 00:02:10,260
Oh, you get better looking every time I see you.

53
00:02:10,480 --> 00:02:11,680
It's puberty, Grandma.

54
00:02:13,400 --> 00:02:16,560
Benjamin Siegfried, don't you ever say that nasty word again.

55
00:02:17,500 --> 00:02:18,100
Puberty?

56
00:02:18,480 --> 00:02:19,680
No, Grandma.

57
00:02:22,200 --> 00:02:25,940
Uh, come on, you two strong men, and get my luggage.

58
00:02:25,940 --> 00:02:28,260
It's that, uh, paisley set over there.

59
00:02:28,540 --> 00:02:29,680
Whatever I can do, Ma.

60
00:02:30,560 --> 00:02:31,240
Oh.

61
00:02:31,740 --> 00:02:34,000
Irma, you look wonderful.

62
00:02:34,480 --> 00:02:36,920
Oh, Maggie, I feel wonderful.

63
00:02:37,220 --> 00:02:39,160
It must have been all that Sierre.

64
00:02:40,200 --> 00:02:45,100
Well, it could have been that or, um...

65
00:02:45,100 --> 00:02:47,140
Uh-huh. Uh-huh-huh-huh.

66
00:02:48,860 --> 00:02:49,540
Uh-huh.

67
00:02:49,540 --> 00:02:49,740
Uh-huh.

68
00:02:49,740 --> 00:02:50,560
You met a man?

69
00:02:50,780 --> 00:02:51,420
No.

70
00:02:51,840 --> 00:02:52,360
Uh-huh.

71
00:02:52,360 --> 00:02:54,340
I met my future husband.

72
00:02:55,660 --> 00:02:56,960
You did what?

73
00:02:58,060 --> 00:02:59,360
Okay, Mom, here we go.

74
00:02:59,660 --> 00:03:00,780
Not a word to Jason.

75
00:03:01,220 --> 00:03:03,200
Now, I want to stop by your place first

76
00:03:03,200 --> 00:03:04,960
because I have some souvenirs for the children.

77
00:03:05,440 --> 00:03:06,420
Oh, no.

78
00:03:07,860 --> 00:03:10,100
I mean, I hope it's something to wear.

79
00:03:14,160 --> 00:03:18,180
Is she amazing when she's laughing and smiling souvenirs for the kids?

80
00:03:18,960 --> 00:03:21,480
And all the while, her heart is breaking.

81
00:03:23,240 --> 00:03:25,480
Show me that smile again.

82
00:03:27,840 --> 00:03:31,620
Don't waste another minute on your crying.

83
00:03:32,080 --> 00:03:35,020
We'll know when he'll be over me.

84
00:03:35,600 --> 00:03:37,480
The test is ready to begin.

85
00:03:39,640 --> 00:03:41,360
Oh, oh, oh, oh.

86
00:03:41,360 --> 00:03:47,400
As long as we got each other, we got the world spinning

87
00:03:47,400 --> 00:03:50,760
right in our hands, baby, you and me.

88
00:03:50,760 --> 00:03:57,180
We gotta be the luckiest dreamers who never quit dreaming

89
00:03:57,180 --> 00:04:00,280
As long as we keep on giving

90
00:04:00,280 --> 00:04:04,960
We can take anything that comes our way

91
00:04:04,960 --> 00:04:09,140
And we're paying the time all the time

92
00:04:09,140 --> 00:04:15,460
We got each other sharing the laughter and love

93
00:04:17,740 --> 00:04:22,520
Share the last bit of love

94
00:04:25,540 --> 00:04:28,980
Oh, Mike, look at this. Dad asked us both to straighten up the house.

95
00:04:29,160 --> 00:04:31,380
Well, Carol, first of all, I do not live here anymore.

96
00:04:31,860 --> 00:04:33,760
Okay? And second of all, what's the big deal?

97
00:04:33,860 --> 00:04:35,220
I mean, it's just Grandma coming over.

98
00:04:35,480 --> 00:04:38,000
I mean, if she doesn't have her glasses on, she'll be lucky to find the couch.

99
00:04:41,340 --> 00:04:43,020
Oh, oh, they're here, okay?

100
00:04:43,020 --> 00:04:46,620
You explained to Dad why you couldn't do this one little favor for him.

101
00:04:46,860 --> 00:04:51,660
One little favor? Carol, for your information, I had my whole Saturday plan, okay?

102
00:04:51,720 --> 00:04:54,400
I mean, this was going to be a day of solid studying.

103
00:04:54,960 --> 00:04:58,160
And now I'm just expected to scrap my education waiting around for Grandma?

104
00:05:01,120 --> 00:05:05,120
Hi, I'm confused. I'm looking for Mike Siever, but he said he lived in an apartment.

105
00:05:06,560 --> 00:05:09,060
Hi, Tony! Hey!

106
00:05:09,960 --> 00:05:10,480
Hi.

107
00:05:10,480 --> 00:05:11,160
Hi.

108
00:05:11,780 --> 00:05:13,920
Hey, listen, didn't you get my message at your dorm?

109
00:05:14,440 --> 00:05:16,580
No, I was in aerobics all morning.

110
00:05:16,860 --> 00:05:17,860
Is that your major?

111
00:05:20,380 --> 00:05:23,520
Listen, listen, we're gonna have to put off tutoring for about an hour or so.

112
00:05:23,760 --> 00:05:26,060
But I thought we were gonna spend the whole day cramming.

113
00:05:27,180 --> 00:05:28,920
Oh, you know, that's what I want to.

114
00:05:29,480 --> 00:05:32,300
But listen, why don't I take you out to my apartment

115
00:05:32,300 --> 00:05:35,300
where you can cool off from your workout while I take care of some business.

116
00:05:35,420 --> 00:05:35,840
Okay, great.

117
00:05:35,940 --> 00:05:37,460
It's out back above the garage.

118
00:05:37,680 --> 00:05:38,880
It's kind of a loft.

119
00:05:39,440 --> 00:05:39,880
Mike!

120
00:05:40,460 --> 00:05:42,560
Uh, listen, after you're done cleaning up the living room here,

121
00:05:42,580 --> 00:05:44,020
why don't you give the kitchen a once over?

122
00:05:45,180 --> 00:05:45,940
Cleanin', lady.

123
00:05:49,820 --> 00:05:51,380
Do you mind if I go take a shower?

124
00:05:52,600 --> 00:05:53,840
Uh, do I mind?

125
00:05:54,380 --> 00:05:56,120
Oh, I insist on it.

126
00:06:00,320 --> 00:06:02,920
Mike, Carol, come and get your souvenirs from Grandma!

127
00:06:06,740 --> 00:06:10,460
Jason, if you ask me one more time how I really feel about the cruise,

128
00:06:10,460 --> 00:06:12,920
I'm gonna take back that souvenir I gave you and Maggie.

129
00:06:13,500 --> 00:06:14,360
Behave yourself, Jason.

130
00:06:14,460 --> 00:06:15,980
I sure don't wanna lose this.

131
00:06:18,300 --> 00:06:21,920
Say, Irma, you haven't seen the baby in three whole weeks,

132
00:06:21,960 --> 00:06:24,460
so why don't you and I go upstairs and you can tell me all about your trip?

133
00:06:24,460 --> 00:06:26,020
Oh, I wanna give out my souvenirs.

134
00:06:26,500 --> 00:06:28,020
Oh, welcome home, Grandma.

135
00:06:28,760 --> 00:06:29,200
Carol!

136
00:06:29,960 --> 00:06:31,040
Oh, la, honey.

137
00:06:32,440 --> 00:06:35,820
Oh, you didn't happen to get me a sombrero, too, did you?

138
00:06:35,960 --> 00:06:37,820
No, honey, I'm afraid I didn't.

139
00:06:38,040 --> 00:06:39,540
Uh, darn it all, anyway.

140
00:06:39,660 --> 00:06:41,340
There's room in here for you, too, Carol.

141
00:06:44,080 --> 00:06:45,580
I did bring you this.

142
00:06:49,840 --> 00:06:50,300
Wow!

143
00:06:51,400 --> 00:06:54,000
Somehow, thank you seems inadequate.

144
00:06:54,960 --> 00:06:56,580
Well, wasn't that fun?

145
00:06:56,600 --> 00:06:58,880
We were gonna go upstairs, and you were gonna tell me all that.

146
00:06:59,080 --> 00:07:00,440
Hey, wait, hold on, Maggie. Where's Mike?

147
00:07:00,440 --> 00:07:02,420
He's cramming in his loft.

148
00:07:03,820 --> 00:07:05,320
Okay, Ben, will you run and get him, please?

149
00:07:08,660 --> 00:07:11,060
Oh, wear this thing later when I'm standing still.

150
00:07:12,580 --> 00:07:16,540
Now, Mom, you really don't have to pretend anymore that you had a good time.

151
00:07:16,700 --> 00:07:21,200
Oh, Jason, you are coming this close to losing that work of art.

152
00:07:21,320 --> 00:07:23,500
Well, if you ask me, Erm, he just stepped over the line,

153
00:07:23,500 --> 00:07:25,320
and you should just take it back to teach him a lesson.

154
00:07:27,200 --> 00:07:29,140
No, we can wait upstairs while we're waiting for him.

155
00:07:30,200 --> 00:07:30,760
Grandma!

156
00:07:31,540 --> 00:07:31,820
Mikey!

157
00:07:32,440 --> 00:07:32,800
Hi!

158
00:07:33,440 --> 00:07:34,780
Hey, how'd you trip to Mexico?

159
00:07:35,500 --> 00:07:36,060
Fabulous.

160
00:07:36,400 --> 00:07:38,960
And for the millionth time, I mean it.

161
00:07:39,580 --> 00:07:42,340
Say, I hear you're living on your own now.

162
00:07:42,440 --> 00:07:43,860
Yeah, well, it was time.

163
00:07:44,160 --> 00:07:46,480
He's 30 feet away in the stupid garage.

164
00:07:48,100 --> 00:07:51,600
Let's see what we have in our happy bag for Mikey.

165
00:07:54,380 --> 00:07:54,400
Hey!

166
00:07:55,120 --> 00:07:55,520
Toro!

167
00:07:56,140 --> 00:07:57,260
Oh, yeah!

168
00:07:59,940 --> 00:08:01,100
Oh, boy!

169
00:08:01,100 --> 00:08:02,120
All right, Grandma.

170
00:08:02,820 --> 00:08:03,400
Yeah.

171
00:08:04,280 --> 00:08:04,860
Hey.

172
00:08:05,900 --> 00:08:06,480
Hey.

173
00:08:06,780 --> 00:08:09,040
Boy, I can't wait to wear this puffy to college.

174
00:08:10,780 --> 00:08:11,960
It's real hip.

175
00:08:12,200 --> 00:08:13,560
Oh, my words exactly.

176
00:08:14,400 --> 00:08:17,540
You know, as much as I would love to hear all about your trip,

177
00:08:17,620 --> 00:08:19,880
I've got to go cuddle up with my studies.

178
00:08:19,880 --> 00:08:20,560
Yeah.

179
00:08:21,500 --> 00:08:23,800
You've certainly changed since I left.

180
00:08:24,160 --> 00:08:25,020
Since this morning.

181
00:08:26,640 --> 00:08:30,340
Well, speaking of changing, you haven't seen the baby in three whole weeks.

182
00:08:30,440 --> 00:08:31,080
I will see you later.

183
00:08:31,080 --> 00:08:31,580
Okay. Bye-bye.

184
00:08:31,600 --> 00:08:33,140
Bye-bye.

185
00:08:33,640 --> 00:08:33,880
Ben.

186
00:08:34,440 --> 00:08:35,420
Hey, Ben, what's the matter?

187
00:08:35,440 --> 00:08:36,380
You look as white as a sheet.

188
00:08:36,780 --> 00:08:37,300
Ben?

189
00:08:38,760 --> 00:08:39,840
Uh, Dad?

190
00:08:40,160 --> 00:08:41,740
Uh, no, uh, Dad.

191
00:08:42,800 --> 00:08:49,860
Uh, I went upstairs to look for Mike, like you said, and I, uh, I was in his apartment,

192
00:08:49,860 --> 00:08:52,500
and there's a woman in his shower.

193
00:08:52,800 --> 00:08:53,320
Naked!

194
00:08:55,100 --> 00:08:55,760
What?

195
00:08:56,260 --> 00:08:56,780
What?

196
00:08:57,180 --> 00:09:00,000
Mike, Dad, I'll handle this.

197
00:09:02,760 --> 00:09:04,080
No you won't!

198
00:09:05,820 --> 00:09:07,480
Now tell me about this gentleman.

199
00:09:08,280 --> 00:09:11,460
Well, there's not much to tell on an eight o'clock show.

200
00:09:13,960 --> 00:09:16,060
Irma, I can't believe what I'm not hearing.

201
00:09:16,480 --> 00:09:18,040
You can't believe it.

202
00:09:18,040 --> 00:09:22,940
Three weeks ago, I stepped on that boat just to stop Jason from saying,

203
00:09:23,380 --> 00:09:26,060
Mom, there is more to life than the new family feud.

204
00:09:27,460 --> 00:09:31,120
I mean, who wants to be reminded this is a world of couples and you're alone?

205
00:09:33,220 --> 00:09:35,300
And then I met Wally.

206
00:09:37,720 --> 00:09:39,940
Second day at sea, we had dinner.

207
00:09:40,900 --> 00:09:43,440
Third day, I...upleached my hair.

208
00:09:45,120 --> 00:09:47,800
And by the fourth, we danced in the moonlight

209
00:09:47,800 --> 00:09:51,320
and by the end of the trip, we decided if he could share a cabin,

210
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:53,080
we could share a home.

211
00:09:53,840 --> 00:09:57,100
Hold on here. Hold on here. You're leaving out a whole bunch of your story.

212
00:09:57,720 --> 00:09:59,320
I certainly did.

213
00:10:01,740 --> 00:10:06,480
Oh, Maggie, Wally is so much better than the family feud.

214
00:10:08,580 --> 00:10:11,620
Norm, I'm so happy for you.

215
00:10:11,860 --> 00:10:16,360
Oh. Oh, it would be perfect if I could just tell Jason.

216
00:10:16,360 --> 00:10:18,480
Well, of course you can tell Jason.

217
00:10:19,020 --> 00:10:21,240
Maggie, you know him as well as I know him,

218
00:10:21,240 --> 00:10:23,240
and you know how close he was to his father.

219
00:10:23,940 --> 00:10:25,420
This isn't gonna be easy for him.

220
00:10:25,460 --> 00:10:27,940
Oh, yes, but when he thinks about it, he'll...

221
00:10:27,940 --> 00:10:29,180
Oh, it is going to be hell.

222
00:10:30,680 --> 00:10:33,300
What kills me, he will never admit when he's upset.

223
00:10:33,380 --> 00:10:34,920
He has been that way since he was a kid.

224
00:10:35,760 --> 00:10:39,640
Tell him the worst news in the world, and his mouth goes into that frozen...

225
00:10:39,640 --> 00:10:42,580
simpleton smile, as if everything's okay.

226
00:10:43,140 --> 00:10:45,840
And his voice goes real high, and he says,

227
00:10:45,840 --> 00:10:50,160
Well, well, well, what an unexpected turn of events.

228
00:10:50,900 --> 00:10:53,200
And then his eye starts twitching.

229
00:10:58,640 --> 00:11:00,420
I don't see why you're having such a cow.

230
00:11:00,540 --> 00:11:02,780
I mean, I told you, I was just tutoring her.

231
00:11:03,840 --> 00:11:05,260
You're having trouble finding that one, aren't you?

232
00:11:06,400 --> 00:11:09,620
Mike, we agreed when you moved out there that from now on, the only-

233
00:11:09,620 --> 00:11:10,820
Wait a minute, hey, why don't you tell me

234
00:11:10,820 --> 00:11:13,280
all about your trip and don't leave anything out?

235
00:11:13,280 --> 00:11:13,500
Wow.

236
00:11:14,960 --> 00:11:16,180
You're not off the hook yet.

237
00:11:17,120 --> 00:11:21,180
Well, Mikey, at first I thought it was going to be pretty boring.

238
00:11:22,080 --> 00:11:23,800
But then I made a friend.

239
00:11:23,960 --> 00:11:25,840
Oh, well, what a trip, Grandma.

240
00:11:27,160 --> 00:11:29,000
Jason, did you hear that?

241
00:11:29,040 --> 00:11:30,080
Your mother made a friend.

242
00:11:30,120 --> 00:11:30,820
Isn't that nice?

243
00:11:30,900 --> 00:11:32,480
Oh, I think that's wonderful.

244
00:11:32,980 --> 00:11:34,220
Does she live around here?

245
00:11:36,080 --> 00:11:37,540
He lives in Manhattan.

246
00:11:39,540 --> 00:11:40,040
Oh.

247
00:11:40,040 --> 00:11:40,080
Oh.

248
00:11:41,680 --> 00:11:42,900
Well, well, well.

249
00:11:44,380 --> 00:11:47,020
So, like, um, the hot boy grandma?

250
00:11:53,840 --> 00:11:56,100
Is he, uh, a good friend?

251
00:11:57,160 --> 00:11:57,780
Mm-hmm.

252
00:11:59,100 --> 00:11:59,920
Well, well, well.

253
00:12:01,680 --> 00:12:04,220
Well, I'd like to meet him sometime.

254
00:12:04,580 --> 00:12:07,940
Well, we could have your mother and her f-friend over to dinner sometime.

255
00:12:09,020 --> 00:12:10,680
Hey, why don't you invite me too?

256
00:12:10,760 --> 00:12:12,180
I'd love to scope this dude out.

257
00:12:14,080 --> 00:12:14,840
That would be lovely.

258
00:12:15,140 --> 00:12:16,400
I should do that sometime.

259
00:12:16,740 --> 00:12:17,060
Tonight.

260
00:12:18,380 --> 00:12:18,740
Tonight?

261
00:12:19,220 --> 00:12:21,820
Well, Jason, I don't think I can get a dinner party ready tonight.

